"""Original robot gripper bench studies; CPU-only geometry."""
from routing_parts import generate_meshes as export_meshes
PARTS=[]
def add(slug,title,dims,values,solid,cut,notes,refs):
 def box(b):return 'translate(['+','.join(map(str,b[:3]))+']) cube(['+','.join(map(str,b[3:]))+']);'
 PARTS.append(dict(slug=slug,title=title,dims=dims,values=values,solid=solid,cut=cut,published='2026-10-17',params='\n'.join(f'{k}={v};' for k,v in values.items()),code='difference(){union(){\n'+'\n'.join(map(box,solid))+'\n}\n'+'\n'.join(map(box,cut))+'\n}',notes=notes+' Original geometry, not a supplier replacement. All mounting apertures are rectangular slots. No physical print, gripping-force, fatigue, friction, retention or environmental tests have been performed. Dimensions are nominal: measure the actual hardware and add process-specific allowance. No powered-robot use, payload rating or standards compliance is established. Use only for unpowered bench fit and layout evaluation.',refs=refs))
REFS=[('Robotiq: custom finger design trials','https://elearning.robotiq.com/course/view.php?id=3&section=9'),('Robotiq: custom fingertip limitations','https://robotiq.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/28281933151507-Custom-Fingertips-on-Hand-E-and-2F-Grippers')]
add('industrial-stepped-gripper-finger-study','Stepped robot gripper finger with slotted mounting foot','24 × 70 × 20 mm; 8 mm body; 12 mm raised contact end',dict(width=24,length=70,body=8,contact_length=24,contact_height=12,slot_width=4.5),
 [('0','0','0','width','length','body'),('0','length-contact_length','body','width','contact_length','contact_height')],
 [('5','6','-1','slot_width','20','body+2'),('width-5-slot_width','6','-1','slot_width','20','body+2'),('7','length-contact_length+6','-1','10','3','body+contact_height+2'),('7','length-9','-1','10','3','body+contact_height+2')],
 'Single generic finger blank. Print two copies for a mirrored opposing layout, then determine the actual gripper adapter separately. Two foot slots span Y6–26 mm with X centers 7.25 and 16.75 mm. The raised contact end is Y46–70 mm and has two 10 × 3 mm strap passages. It matches the separately downloadable pad outline, with no positive pad latch. Fixed offsets must be reviewed after parameter edits. No motor, linkage, sensor, fasteners or proprietary mounting pattern is included. Finger length changes leverage at the gripper base; consult actual manufacturer limits before designing an adapter. Print broad 24 × 70 mm back face on the bed, step upward.',REFS)
add('industrial-replaceable-gripper-contact-pad','Replaceable robot gripper contact pad with strap slots','24 × 24 × 5 mm; two 10 × 3 mm strap slots; three shallow relief grooves',dict(width=24,length=24,thickness=5,groove_depth=0.6),
 [('0','0','0','width','length','thickness')],
 [('7','6','-1','10','3','thickness+2'),('7','15','-1','10','3','thickness+2')]+[('2',str(y),'thickness-groove_depth','width-4','0.8','groove_depth+1') for y in [3,11.6,20]],
 'A separate contact-pad geometry study matching the 24 × 24 mm end of the stepped finger. Two strap slots align when its origin is translated by Y46/Z20 relative to the finger. Relief grooves do not establish extra friction or gripping force. Separate straps are required; routing them over the contact face can interfere with the workpiece. TPU may be evaluated for compliance using the filament supplier settings; material suitability and retention are unverified. No adhesive or fastener is included. Print flat back down and grooves upward. Measure the assembled stack and evaluate creep and contact pressure on an unpowered bench.',REFS)
add('industrial-gripper-finger-storage-rack','Robot gripper finger storage rack with three open pockets','90 × 50 × 25 mm; three 26 × 10 mm open pockets; 4 mm floor',dict(length=90,width=50,height=25,floor=4,pocket_width=26,pocket_depth=10),
 [('0','0','0','length','width','height')],
 [(str(x),'20','floor','pocket_width','pocket_depth','height') for x in [3,32,61]]+[('8','5','-1','5','8','height+2'),('77','5','-1','5','8','height+2')],
 'Three pockets store loose generic finger blanks upright on a bench, not an assembled robot end effector. Each 26 × 10 mm pocket leaves 2 mm nominal total width and thickness allowance around a measured 24 × 8 mm plain finger end. The raised finger end remains above the rack. Pocket origins X3,32,61/Y20 mm, depth21 mm. Floor thickness is 4 mm. Two through mounting slots accept separately selected hardware and washers. Fit, tipping stability and retention are untested; do not use this as a robot docking station or tool changer. Print flat underside down, pockets upward.',REFS)
SOURCE_REFERENCES={p['slug']:p['refs'] for p in PARTS}
def generate_meshes():export_meshes(PARTS)
if __name__=='__main__':generate_meshes()
